[{:db/id "q-342363/field-1/31063f58997914912da54fb93e61dddc91e3b09c0a6369b398a0e56691bd6722" :answer/id #uuid "3e629624-0acf-5467-9cf2-d1187d2ce9f6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x}{3}+\\frac{16}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342363/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "974c793b-3d07-5517-946e-8468b4b17481" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-342363/field-1/31063f58997914912da54fb93e61dddc91e3b09c0a6369b398a0e56691bd6722" :answer-field/choices ["q-342363/field-1/31063f58997914912da54fb93e61dddc91e3b09c0a6369b398a0e56691bd6722"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-342363" :question/id #uuid "8675848b-359e-5358-9ed8-913d5be71171" :question/math-academy-id "q-342363" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent to the curve $y=4\\sqrt[3]{x}$ at the point $(8,8).$\n\n$y=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=4\\sqrt[3]{x}.$ Computing the derivative ${f}^{′}(x)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4\\sqrt[3]{x}) \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\sqrt[3]{x}) \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{1/3}) \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}{x}^{-2/3} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe then compute ${f}^{′}(8)$, which gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(8) & =\\frac{4}{3\\sqrt[3]{{8}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3\\sqrt[3]{64}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3\\cdot 4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we use the point-slope form with $m=\\frac{1}{3}$ and the coordinates of our point $(8,8),$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-8 & =\\frac{1}{3}(x-8) \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{3}x-\\frac{8}{3}+8 \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{3}x+\\frac{16}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-342363/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uui